'''This project contains:

Backend (Django):

Django REST Framework for APIs

CORS enabled

WhiteNoise static serving

UserData CRUD API

Frontend (React):

Fetches user data from Django API

Built and served through Django in production

Both projects live inside the same root directory for easy management.

📁 Project Structure
myproject/
│
├── backend/
│   ├── api/                     ← Django app (Models, Views, Serializers)
│   ├── backend/                 ← Project settings + URLs
│   │   ├── templates/           ← React index.html
│   │   ├── static/              ← React static JS/CSS files
│   │   ├── settings.py
│   │   ├── urls.py
│   │   └── views.py
│   ├── db.sqlite3
│   └── manage.py
│
└── frontend/                    ← React application
    ├── build/                   ← Production build output
    ├── src/
    ├── public/
    └── package.json

🔧 Backend Setup (Django)
1. Install requirements
pip install djangorestframework django-cors-headers whitenoise

2. Add apps in backend/settings.py
INSTALLED_APPS = [
    'django.contrib.admin',
    'django.contrib.auth',
    'django.contrib.contenttypes',
    'django.contrib.sessions',
    'django.contrib.messages',
    'django.contrib.staticfiles',
    'api',
    'rest_framework',
    'corsheaders',
]

3. Middleware setup
MIDDLEWARE = [
    'django.middleware.security.SecurityMiddleware',
    'corsheaders.middleware.CorsMiddleware',
    'django.contrib.sessions.middleware.SessionMiddleware',
    'django.middleware.common.CommonMiddleware',
    'django.middleware.csrf.CsrfViewMiddleware',
    'django.contrib.auth.middleware.AuthenticationMiddleware',
    'django.contrib.messages.middleware.MessageMiddleware',
    'django.middleware.clickjacking.XFrameOptionsMiddleware',
    'whitenoise.middleware.WhiteNoiseMiddleware',
]


Enable CORS:

CORS_ALLOW_ALL_ORIGINS = True

4. Django Template & Static Configuration
TEMPLATES = [
    {
        'BACKEND': 'django.template.backends.django.DjangoTemplates',
        'DIRS': [os.path.join(BASE_DIR, 'backend/templates')],
        'APP_DIRS': True,
        'OPTIONS': {
            'context_processors': [
                'django.template.context_processors.request',
                'django.contrib.auth.context_processors.auth',
                'django.contrib.messages.context_processors.messages',
            ],
        },
    },
]

STATIC_URL = '/static/'
STATICFILES_DIRS = [
    os.path.join(BASE_DIR, 'backend/static'),
]
STATIC_ROOT = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, 'staticfiles')

🗄 Database Model

api/models.py

class UserData(models.Model):
    first_name = models.CharField(max_length=100)
    last_name = models.CharField(max_length=100)
    email = models.EmailField(unique=True)
    phone_number = models.CharField(max_length=15)
    age = models.IntegerField()

    GENDER_CHOICES = [
        ('male', 'Male'),
        ('female', 'Female'),
        ('other', 'Other'),
    ]

    gender = models.CharField(max_length=10, choices=GENDER_CHOICES)


Run migrations:

python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate

🔄 API Layer
Serializer (api/serializers.py)
class UserDataSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
    class Meta:
        model = UserData
        fields = '__all__'

ViewSet (api/views.py)
class UserDataViewSet(viewsets.ModelViewSet):
    queryset = UserData.objects.all()
    serializer_class = UserDataSerializer

API URL Routing (api/urls.py)
router = DefaultRouter()
router.register(r'users', UserDataViewSet)

urlpatterns = [
    path('', include(router.urls)),
]

Main URLs (backend/backend/urls.py)
urlpatterns = [
    path('admin/', admin.site.urls),
    path('api/', include('api.urls')),
]

🎨 Frontend Setup (React)

Inside frontend/:

Start dev server:

npm start

📡 Connecting React to Django API
useEffect(() => {
  fetchUsersData();
}, []);

const fetchUsersData = async () => {
  const data = await fetch('http://localhost:8000/api/users/');
  const res = await data.json();
  setUsersData(res);
};

🏗 Building React for Production
cd frontend
npm run build

Copy build files to Django:

✔ Copy build/index.html → backend/backend/templates/index.html
✔ Copy build/static → backend/backend/static/

This allows Django to serve React.

🔥 Serve React from Django

Create backend/backend/views.py:

class ReactAppView(TemplateView):
    template_name = "index.html"


Add catch-all route in backend/backend/urls.py:

urlpatterns += [
    re_path(r'^.*$', ReactAppView.as_view(), name='react'),
]


Now Django serves:

/api/... → backend API

all other routes → React app

🧪 Run the Full Application
cd backend
python manage.py runserver


Visit:

http://localhost:8000/


You will see the React frontend served by Django.

🔄 Updating Frontend After Changes

Whenever React UI changes:

npm run build
copy build → Django static + template folders


Django automatically serves the new React version.

🎉 Project Completed Successfully

You now have:

✔ Django backend (API)
✔ React frontend
✔ Both inside one project
✔ One-server deployment model
✔ No CORS issues
✔ Production optimized setup'''